{"assignees":[],"author":{"id":"U_kgDOEBSQMQ","is_bot":false,"login":"eliottreich","name":""},"body":"### GitHub Repository URL\n\nhttps://github.com/eliottreich/taskbounty-mcp-server\n\n### Logo Image\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/eliottreich/taskbounty-mcp-server/main/logo-400.png (400x400 PNG)\n\n### Reason for Addition\n\nTaskBounty Autopilot fixes your bugs while you sleep. Connect a repo, file an issue anywhere your team already files them (GitHub, Sentry, Linear, Jira, Slack, email), and wake up to a verified pull request in your morning digest. Every PR passes your full test suite in a sandbox before it reaches you. First verified PR wins, multiple solvers attempt every bounty. 14 days plus 5 verified PRs free, no card to install. Solo $49/mo, Team $29/seat (min 5), free tier on per-bounty.\n\nThis MCP server is the in-Claude / in-Cline interface to that platform. 11 tools across two flows. Posters create and fund bounties, list their tasks, review submissions, and award winners. Solvers list open bounties matching the repo they are working in, fetch full bounty detail, request short-lived read-only clone access for private repos, submit PRs, and check verification status.\n\n### Installation Testing\n\nTested install path: `npx -y taskbounty-mcp-server`. Set `TASKBOUNTY_API_KEY=tb_live_...` in env for write tools. Read-only tools (list open bounties, get bounty detail) work without a key. `npx -y taskbounty-mcp-server --help` prints install instructions, env vars, and a Cline-ready JSON config snippet.\n\n- [x] I have tested that Cline can successfully set up this server using only the README.md\n- [x] The server is stable and ready for public use\n\n### Security disclosures\n\n- No telemetry. The MCP server only calls https://www.task-bounty.com/api/v1/* on user action.\n- Code never leaves the E2B sandbox during verification. Solver code runs in isolated VMs against a clone of the target repo. The MCP server itself never reads, writes, or transmits user source code.\n- API key handling: TASKBOUNTY_API_KEY is read from env at startup, sent only over HTTPS to api.task-bounty.com as a Bearer token. Never logged.\n- Read-only clone tokens minted via `request_repo_access` are short-lived (~1h) and read-only. Push happens through the solver's own fork.\n\n### Additional Information\n\nnpm: https://www.npmjs.com/package/taskbounty-mcp-server\nDocs: https://www.task-bounty.com/docs/mcp?utm_source=cline-marketplace&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=directory\nLicense: MIT\nAuthor: Eliott Reich, founder of TaskBounty (eliott@task-bounty.com)\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDON51qis8AAAABCfwQ2w","author":{"login":"zp6"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Working on this. Wallet: zp6","createdAt":"2026-05-15T18:54:52Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/cline/mcp-marketplace/issues/1571#issuecomment-4462481627","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"createdAt":"2026-05-15T11:29:46Z","labels":[],"state":"OPEN","title":"[Server Submission]: TaskBounty MCP Server","updatedAt":"2026-05-15T18:54:52Z","url":"https://github.com/cline/mcp-marketplace/issues/1571"}
